<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 7,607 tonnes of zinc.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 7,607 tonnes of zinc.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 16,771,534 pounds or 7,607 tonnes of prime western and high grade zinc for $10,506,685.</p>
<p>The winning bidders were Sipi Metals, Brown Industries, Ingot Metal Co, Tally Metal Sales, Frontier Hot Dip Galv, Hochschild Partners, and Allied Deals.</p>
<p>The next bid opening is on June 17.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
